From c7022662a6f494d15a7931e744a25e9cb5b9877e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:58:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] MSC log over UDP (-DMSC_LOG=ON) and a "status" command on UDP
 6869

At power-on the Z sometimes says it cannot boot from the disk, when it
reads the boot area before the Pico has Wi-Fi, SMB and the HDS.

-DMSC_LOG=ON (off by default): send one line per USB MSC command to
MSC_LOG_HOST (default 192.168.1.108) UDP 6870, to see what the Z reads,
when, and what we answer, and whether a soft reset re-reads the boot
sector:

  <seq> <start ms> <took ms> R|W <USB LBA> n=<sectors> <where> [err] [head=<8 bytes>] [tur=N] [skip=N]
  <seq> <ms> C op=<SCSI opcode> lun=N      (TEST UNIT READY only counted)
  <seq> <ms> M <event>                     (sysstatus, SMB, HDS opened, vd_sync wait/done)
  <seq> <ms> U mount|umount

<where> is the virtual FAT area or id<SCSI ID>:<HDS LBA>. Records go
into a ring from the USB task and a small task sends them once Wi-Fi is
up, so the reads before the connection are kept. 300 records after each
USB mount and after each 2 s pause; ID 6's netpipe/scsiremote band is
only counted.

HID builds: "status" on UDP 6869 answers one line from the existing
state (sysstatus, diskinfo, rootpath) plus MSC sector counters, netpipe
exchanges and the accelerator:

  ok stat=5 wifi=up ip=192.168.1.118 rssi=-55 smb=mounted hds0=open remote0=ok
     uptime=812s usb=mounted reads=1234 writes=56 npd=789 accel=ready/3 hid=ok heap=60000

It is answered by its own task, so it works while a key command runs and
while the USB task waits in vd_sync for the SMB connection. The 6869
socket now opens before USB starts instead of after Wi-Fi is up.

With HID_KEYBOARD and MSC_LOG off the binary is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
